Hello,
I know a lot of you thought we were dead. Lack of communication and updates from our side. Even a simple 3-word message ex. "we are alive". We apologize for that and it's time for changes. We forgot what "Early Access" is about.

"Early Access is a tool to develop your game with the community by giving them access to your title before it is officially released.

"Early Access is a unique development model that allows games to be played as they progress towards a full release. Early Access encourages ongoing updates from developers while letting players participate in direct feedback through gameplay and community involvement."

Starting today we are releasing the "Beta" branch which is different from the previous one. You will be able to test everything. We will push there every single update, with even the smallest changelog. You will be able to have fun, going mad or crying - as this version can be unstable.

Starting now "BETA" branch is now available for everyone in the game settings. You can start playing Multiplayer, and test a lot of changes & improvements (ex. fish stopping at 0 stamina). 

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/36994199/2bea3361465e1f5a4a6de9e2da9ebc26ee041a1f.gif

You can report all issues you encounter via in-game F5 or in the Steam Discussions:
https://steamcommunity.com/app/1136380/discussions/2/


 PUBLIC BETA | HOW TO PLAY? [olist]
 Right-click on the game from the library page and select "Properties".
 Click on the "BETAS" tab.
 Select from the dropdown list “public beta”
 Press OK.[/olist]
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/36994199/b1d6783d211e63456d816d6f10ba81e3d0dc0361.png

SAVE FILES INSTRUCTIONS
Instructions for players starting open tests:
 Close the game.
 Back up the .CFG and .UFS2 files located in "AppData\LocalLow\MasterCode\Ultimate Fishing Simulator 2\Saves".
 Switch to the test branch on Steam.
 Create a new profile in the game. It's also possible to clone your profile from the release branch using Steam Cloud, but there is a chance of incompatibility.
Instructions for players finishing open tests and returning to the release branch:
 Close the game.
 Switch to the release branch on Steam.
 Launch the game; the original save will be selected automatically. You can use the save from the test branch via Steam Cloud at your own risk, but there is a chance of incompatibility.
Instructions for players in case of any save issues:
 Close the game.
 Go to "AppData\LocalLow\MasterCode\Ultimate Fishing Simulator 2\Saves".
 Replace the .CFG and .UFS2 files with your backup.
 Launch the game, avoiding the button that downloads the save from Steam Cloud in the profiles panel.

